lic>C. elegans</italic> embryos. <source>Development.</source> <volume>133</volume>:<fpage>3507</fpage>&#x02013;3516.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16899536</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Siegrist, S.E., and C.Q. Doe. <year>2005</year>. Microtubule-induced Pins/Galphai cortical polarity in <italic>Drosophila</italic> neuroblasts. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>123</volume>:<fpage>1323</fpage>&#x02013;1335.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16377571</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Siegrist, S.E., and C.Q. Doe. <year>2007</year>. Microtubule-induced cortical cell polarity. <source>Genes Dev.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>483</fpage>&#x02013;496.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17344411</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Sonneville, R., and P. Gonczy. <year>2004</year>. zyg-11 and cul-2 regulate progression through meiosis II and polarity establishment in C. elegans. <source>Development.</source> <volume>131</volume>:<fpage>3527</fpage>&#x02013;3543.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15215208</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Tsai, M.-C., and J. Ahringer. <year>2007</year>. Microtubules are involved in anterior-posterior axis formation in <italic>C. elegans</italic> embryos. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>179</volume>:<fpage>397</fpage>&#x02013;402.</citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Wallenfang, M.R., and G. Seydoux. <year>2000</year>. Polarization of the anterior-posterior axis of <italic>C. elegans</italic> is a microtubule-directed process. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>408</volume>:<fpage>89</fpage>&#x02013;92.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11081513</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Wittmann, T., and C.M. Waterman-Storer. <year>2001</year>. Cell motility: can Rho GTPases and microtubules point the way? <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>3795</fpage>&#x02013;3803.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11719546</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>